<section class="audience">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="audience-content">
      <h2>Built for engineering teams who need parts that fit</h2>
      <p>
        Hardware engineers, mechanical designers, and product teams who need reliable CAD geometry — not creative prompts.
        Parts that mate with existing assemblies. Components that clear tolerances. Brackets that actually mount.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you're tired of LLMs that hallucinate dimensions or dump broken scripts, Kala is the structured path from brief to STEP.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .audience {
    padding: var(--section-padding-desktop) 0;
    background: var(--bg-muted);
  }

  .audience-content {
    max-width: var(--prose-max-width);
    margin: 0 auto;
    text-align: center;
  }

  h2 {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-8);
  }

  p {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
    margin: 0 auto var(--space-6);
  }

  p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .audience {
      padding: var(--section-padding-mobile) 0;
    }

    p {
      font-size: 1rem;
    }
  }
</style>
